{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791366961,"nonce":"Mt7DMhZ2toT/gkjXzw7PcYn4JtA=","title":"Unary numeric operators on nullable scalars use the box representation","message":"At 179b21de94f48b4c16413829cd52c107425fca15, var a:Null\u003cInt\u003e=10; ~a crashes after bitwise complement is emitted directly on the box pointer. MIR from /tmp/rayzor-target-static-probe-mir.log shows not $2 followed by haxe_unbox_int_ptr on the resulting inverted address. The nullable arithmetic subset without complement passes; /tmp/rayzor-nullable-arithmetic/NullableArithmetic.hx reproduces the crash when complement is added. TestOps.testNullOps exposes the same defect once target.static is enabled.\n\nNative Haxe Context.typeof reports Int for -a and ~a with a:Null\u003cInt\u003e, Float for -f with f:Null\u003cFloat\u003e, and Int for ~d with d:Dynamic (probe /tmp/rayzor-nullable-arithmetic/UnaryTypes.hx). The typer currently returns the nullable operand type for negation/complement, and MIR opens no nullable numeric payload before a non-mutating unary operator. Dynamic complement similarly needs its integer payload, not a pointer complement.\n\nRegression fixture NullableUnaryArithmetic.hx covers local nullable Int and Float, zero, fields, array elements, typedefs, Dynamic complement and inferred result types. Native Haxe --interp passes. Preserve increment/decrement result and writeback behavior, and abstract operator overloads.","files":null}]}